{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mic-5-1","title":"Micah 5:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The birth of Christ. 4 His kingdom. 8 His conquest.</p>\n<p>gather. De 28:49; 2Ki 24:2; Isa 8:9; 10:6; Jer 4:7; 25:9; Joe 3:9; Hab 1:6 Hab 3:16 he hath. De 28:51-57; 2Ki 25:1-3; Eze 21:21,22; 24:2; Lu 19:43,44 they. Job 16:10; La 3:30; Mt 5:39; 26:67; 27:30; Joh 18:22; 19:3; Ac 23:2 2Co 11:20 judge. 1Sa 8:5,6; Isa 33:22; Am 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-2","title":"Micah 5:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>But thou. Mt 2:6; Joh 7:42 Ephratah. Ge 35:19; 48:7 Ephrath. Ru 4:11; 1Sa 17:12; 1Ch 2:50,51,54; 4:4; Ps 132:6 among. 1Sa 10:19; 23:23 thousands. Ex 18:21,25; De 1:15; 1Sa 8:12; 17:18 yet. Isa 11:1; 53:2; Eze 17:22-24; Am 9:11; Lu 2:4-7; 1Co 1:27,28 that is. Ge 49:10; 1Ch 5:2; Isa 9:6,7; Jer 13:5,6; Eze 34:23,24; 37:22-25 Zec 9:9; Mt 28:18; Lu 1:31-33; 23:2,38; Joh 19:14-22; Re 19:16 whose. Ps 90:2; 102:25-27; Pr 8:22; Joh 1:1-3; Col 1:17; Heb 13:8; 1Jo 1:1 Re 1:11-18; 2:8; 21:6 everlasting. or, the days of eternity.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-3","title":"Micah 5:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Therefore. 7:13; Ho 2:9,14 give. 6:14; 1Ki 14:16; 2Ch 30:7; Ho 11:8 she. 4:10; Isa 66:7,8; Mt 1:21; Re 12:1,2 then. 4:7; Isa 10:20,21; 11:11; Jer 31:1,7-9; Ro 9:27,28; 11:4-6 his. Mt 12:50; 25:40; Ro 8:29; Heb 1:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-4","title":"Micah 5:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>stand. 7:14; Ps 23:1,2; Isa 40:10,11; 49:9,10; Eze 34:22-24; Joh 10:27-30 feed. or, rule. Mt 2:6; *marg: in the majesty. Ex 23:21; 1Ch 29:11,12; Ps 45:3-6; 72:19; 93:1; 145:12; Mt 25:31 Joh 5:22-29; 10:38; 14:9-11; Re 1:13-18 the Lord. Joh 20:17; Eph 1:3 shall abide. Mt 16:18; 1Pe 1:5; Jude 1:1 shall he be great. Ps 22:27; 72:8; 98:3; Isa 49:5; 52:10; Zec 9:10; Lu 1:32; Re 11:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-5","title":"Micah 5:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>this. Ps 72:7; Isa 9:6,7; Zec 9:10; Lu 2:14; Joh 14:27; 16:33; Eph 2:14-17 Col 1:20,21 when the. Isa 7:14; 8:7-10; 37:31-36; 65:8; Jer 33:15 then. Isa 44:28; 59:19; Zec 1:18-21; 9:13; 10:3; 12:6; Re 17:14; 19:14 seven. Job 5:19; Pr 6:16; 30:18,29; Ec 11:2; Am 1:3,6 principal men. Heb. princes of men.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-6","title":"Micah 5:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>they. Isa 14:2; 33:1; Na 2:11-13; 3:1-3 waste. Heb. eat up. the land of Nimrod. Ge 10:9-11; *marg: in the entrances thereof. or, with her own naked swords.thus. Isa 14:25; Lu 1:71,74 the Assyrian. 2Ki 15:29; 17:3-5; 18:9-15; 19:32-35; 2Ch 33:11; Isa 10:5-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-7","title":"Micah 5:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the remnant. 3,8; Eze 14:22; Joe 2:32; Am 5:15; Zep 3:13; Ro 11:5,6 as a dew. De 32:2; Jud 6:36; Ps 72:6; 110:3; Isa 32:15; 44:3; 66:19; Eze 47:1 Ho 6:3; 14:5; Zec 14:8; Mt 28:19; Ac 9:15; 11:15; 13:46 Ro 11:12; 15:19,20; 1Co 3:6 tarrieth. Isa 55:10; Jer 14:22; Ac 16:9; Ro 9:30; 10:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-8","title":"Micah 5:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>as a lion. 4:13; Ps 2:8-12; 110:5,6; Isa 41:15,16; Ob 1:18,19; Zec 9:15; 10:5 Zec 12:3; Mt 10:14; Ac 18:6; 2Co 2:15-17 sheep. or, goats. and none. Ps 50:22; Heb 2:3; 12:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-9","title":"Micah 5:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>hand. Ps 21:8; 106:26; Isa 1:25; 11:14; 14:2-4; 26:11; 33:10; 37:36 Lu 19:27; 1Co 15:25; Re 19:13-21; 20:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-10","title":"Micah 5:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>that I. Ps 20:7,8; 33:16,17; Jer 3:23; Ho 1:7; 14:3; Zec 9:10 will cut.This seems to refer to those happy times when the Jews shall be converted and restored to their own land: and all their enemies being destroyed, they shall have no further need of cavalry or fenced cities.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-11","title":"Micah 5:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>and throw. Isa 2:12-17; Eze 38:11; Zec 4:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-12","title":"Micah 5:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Isa 2:6-8,18,20; 8:19,20; 27:9; Zec 13:2-4; Re 19:20; 22:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-13","title":"Micah 5:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>graven. Isa 17:7,8; Eze 6:9; 36:25; 37:23; Ho 2:16,17; 14:3,8 standing images. or, statues. no. Isa 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-14","title":"Micah 5:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>cities. or, enemies. 11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-5-15","title":"Micah 5:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>8; Ps 149:7; 2Th 1:8</p>"}]}